From 28f9add258a233134f258f15209d364722f953ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:13:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/34] demux: mkv: clamp a seek to the end of an ordered
 edition

For an ordered edition the duration of the edition is the virtual stop
time of its last chapter:

    i_duration = vchapters[ vchapters.size() - 1 ]->i_mk_virtual_stop_time;

and virtual_segment_c::Duration() hands that to the demuxer, so a seek to
100% asks for exactly that timestamp. ContainsTimestamp() is half open,

    return ( time >= i_mk_virtual_start_time && time < i_mk_virtual_stop_time );

so no chapter ever contains it, and the fallback only returns the last
chapter when its stop time is negative - which an ordered edition's is
not. getChapterbyTimecode() therefore returns NULL, virtual_segment_c::
Seek() returns false, and the seek fails outright instead of landing at
the end.

Clamp to the last chapter when the requested time is within it, keeping
the existing behaviour for a last chapter with no known stop time.

(cherry picked from commit 4a22573cb21fb99f3220f8e6c7791ff152e6f3dd)
---
 modules/demux/mkv/virtual_segment.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mkv/virtual_segment.cpp b/modules/demux/mkv/virtual_segment.cpp
index 4070d64373..336edb91ef 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mkv/virtual_segment.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/mkv/virtual_segment.cpp
@@ -412,8 +412,13 @@ virtual_chapter_c* virtual_edition_c::getChapterbyTimecode( int64_t time )
     {
         virtual_chapter_c* last_chapter = vchapters.back();
 
+        /* The virtual stop time of the last chapter is also the duration of
+         * the edition, and ContainsTimestamp() is half open, so a seek to the
+         * very end - a seek to 100%, for instance - matches no chapter at all.
+         * Clamp it to the last chapter instead of failing the seek. */
         if( last_chapter->i_mk_virtual_start_time <= time &&
-            last_chapter->i_mk_virtual_stop_time < 0 )
+            ( last_chapter->i_mk_virtual_stop_time < 0 ||
+              time <= last_chapter->i_mk_virtual_stop_time ) )
         {
             return last_chapter;
         }
